                        "entry_id": "11a0c3bf-8ac2-3528-92ae-e70ccba06a7f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui est entrelacé avec un autre corps ou élément."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae6d7dac-50f9-4002-ab29-b9bdf68a0434",
                                "sense_id": "a64e1093-f8b8-3a37-b032-80b255b82988",
                                "text": "Le processus symplectique […] forme désormais une pièce distincte."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "313fb29e-961b-40de-8429-11891b0cde02",
                        "source_entry_id": "11a0c3bf-8ac2-3528-92ae-e70ccba06a7f",
                        "source_sense_id": "a64e1093-f8b8-3a37-b032-80b255b82988",
                        "target_lang_word": "symplectic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "symplectic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57690214-ee23-366b-9a64-6efff1401ea6",
                                        "entry_id": "9f30b58f-02a6-3683-a850-27c320b1637b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Placed in or among, as if woven together."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39ba6510-a041-3676-abbb-c410d5515aaf",
                                        "entry_id": "9f30b58f-02a6-3683-a850-27c320b1637b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Whose characteristic abelian subgroups are cyclic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2720ea2c-91da-3ea5-923a-947c9ff62954",
                                        "entry_id": "9f30b58f-02a6-3683-a850-27c320b1637b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That is alternating and nondegenerate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4923f693-ecfe-3e90-b6f8-df26f96ece8d",
                                        "entry_id": "9f30b58f-02a6-3683-a850-27c320b1637b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That is equipped with an alternating nondegenerate bilinear form."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "40939c38-4b83-389c-aeaf-cdedcf6b044a",
                                        "entry_id": "9f30b58f-02a6-3683-a850-27c320b1637b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to (the geometry of) a differentiable manifold equipped with a closed nondegenerate bilinear form."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98b60b6a-d437-47d0-aceb-21569619c622",
                                                "sense_id": "40939c38-4b83-389c-aeaf-cdedcf6b044a",
                                                "text": "There exist interesting and unexplored relations between symplectic geometry and the theory of critical points of holomorphic functions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "adfc94b9-341d-407d-ab21-e7768908fa7a",
                                                "sense_id": "40939c38-4b83-389c-aeaf-cdedcf6b044a",
                                                "text": "1997, C. H. Cushman-de Vries (translator), Richard H. Cushman, Gijs M. Tuynman (translation editors), Jean-Marie Souriau, Structure of Dynamical Systems: A Symplectic View of Physics, Springer Science & Business Media (Birkhäuser)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64a80154-9d52-449b-8eb7-53f3faccf84e",
                                                "sense_id": "40939c38-4b83-389c-aeaf-cdedcf6b044a",
                                                "text": "2003, Fabrizio Catanese, Gang Tian (editors), Symplectic 4-Manifolds and Algebraic Surfaces: Lectures given at the C.I.M.E Summer School, Springer, Lecture Notes in Mathematics No. 1938."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0cbf16e2-9f98-4574-8da4-8635ac1d79db",
                                                "sense_id": "40939c38-4b83-389c-aeaf-cdedcf6b044a",
                                                "text": "In symplectic geometry, there is a notion of fibrations #92;pi#58;P#92;rightarrowM with a symplectic manifold F as fiber, where the structure group is the group of (exact) Hamiltonian symplectomorphisms of the fiber. These are called symplectic fibrations. If the base manifold (M,#92;omega#95;M) is also symplectic, there is a weak coupling construction, originally due to Thurston, of defining a symplectic structure on the total space P."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d899434d-7eae-3ef5-bb22-41b5921ba663",
                                        "entry_id": "9f30b58f-02a6-3683-a850-27c320b1637b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That moves in the same direction as a system of synchronized waves."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5174c217-cd6a-3e82-9585-da4a86a1e7b8",
                                        "entry_id": "9f30b58f-02a6-3683-a850-27c320b1637b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to a symplectite; symplectitic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "symplectic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1e836d84-c823-3cca-bb3b-3bbb38514c97",
                                        "entry_id": "3734acfc-ed82-3594-8111-9ab724e04e4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A symplectic bilinear form, manifold, geometry, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87091acd-c222-40e2-a38f-f102ca4d6ddf",
                                                "sense_id": "1e836d84-c823-3cca-bb3b-3bbb38514c97",
                                                "text": "The structure of stable symplectics on finite dimensional spaces has been studied by Krein [8], Gelfand & Lidskii [9], and Moser [10] in work of considerable practical importance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e8f140b-dd3c-3843-b3e1-12bc5af36eaf",
                                        "entry_id": "3734acfc-ed82-3594-8111-9ab724e04e4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bone in the teleostean fishes that forms the lower ossification of the suspensorium, and which articulates below with the quadrate bone by which it is firmly held."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3b18507-ef27-4442-9610-99ec4d5d66e2",
                                                "sense_id": "5e8f140b-dd3c-3843-b3e1-12bc5af36eaf",
                                                "text": "The symplectics (9) consist of a somewhat curved central triangular portion with the base upward, and anteriorly and posteriorly from this extends a wing-like process."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6356fbda-df12-475b-beaa-ed16fe139d54",
                                                "sense_id": "5e8f140b-dd3c-3843-b3e1-12bc5af36eaf",
                                                "text": "The symplectics (Fig. 8, sym) are thin slender bones placed vertically in between the quadrates and the hyomandibulars."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "148a1536-3bd0-4b4d-a69b-a5eb2491a58b",
                                                "sense_id": "5e8f140b-dd3c-3843-b3e1-12bc5af36eaf",
                                                "text": "In many teleosts, on the other hand, including the catfishes, the symplectics have been entirely lost."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
